  "caption": {
    "hashtags": [],
    "public_preview": null,
    "text": "Leave a ❤️ below to affirm! The older I get, the more I realize the little things are often the biggest things, and the biggest things are usually the simplest things. Reassurance. Consistency. Kept promises. Feeling chosen. Feeling emotionally safe. Being around people who handle your humanity with care.\n\nAt this point in my life, these things feel less like luxuries and more like non-negotiables. The world is already hard enough. Our nervous systems carry too much for love, friendship, community, or daily life to feel like constant confusion, uncertainty, or survival mode.\n\nI think real alignment brings a certain kind of softness with it. A certain kind of clarity and peace. And if that quality of care isn’t present, then neither is my presence. \n\nI hope your flowers bloom beautifully this season. Protect yourself. 🌷\n\nWritten by @williegreene_",
    "word_count": 139
  },
